# The terminal itself.
#
# Here rather than in modules/apps -- where it lived until this module existed
# -- so that enabling ghostty gets you the app AND the config it reads. A cask
# in one module and its configuration in another is a module you can switch on
# and have nothing happen.
#
# The FONT it renders with is deliberately not here. `font-jetbrains-mono-nerd-font`
# stays in modules/apps because zellij's bar and the starship prompt draw with
# the same glyphs, so it is not this module's to own.
#
# `auto_updates true` on the cask side: Homebrew will not upgrade this, Ghostty
# updates itself. config.ghostty sets `auto-update = check` to make that a
# prompt rather than a surprise.
cask "ghostty"
